+# Nuur security backport
+
+This package starts from the published `sprintf-js@1.0.3` archive. Nuur adds
+format-width and precision validation for
+[CVE-2026-97058 / GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c),
+which affects every release through 1.1.3 and has no patched npm release as of
+2026-10-08.
+
+Numeric precision is limited to the ECMAScript conversion bounds (0–100, or
+1–100 for `%g`). String precision and field width are capped at 10,000 to
+prevent attacker-controlled allocations while preserving ordinary formatting.
+Invalid specifiers fail deterministically during parsing with `SyntaxError`
+instead of reaching native numeric conversions or string allocation helpers.
+
